ask-boston
==========

Built for RAG the City, The Open Accelerator, Boston — August 22, 2026.

Derived from the official starter repository:
  rag-the-city-starter — https://github.com/holzerjm/rag-the-city-starter
  Licensed Apache-2.0. Copied and modified here:
    baseline/naive_rag.py, baseline/split_corpus.py  (unmodified; kept as
      the measurement baseline)
    boston/download.py, boston/ingest.py, boston/query.py
    civic/_hybrid_reference.py  (from track_a_engine/hybrid_search.py)
    eval/judge.py  (from lab0_millbrook/judge.py; modified to accept a
      --pipeline argument so any system can be graded)
    lab0_boston/  (corpus, eval questions, design notes — unmodified)

Lab 0 corpus, "The Fort Point Files": a work of fiction created for RAG
education. Characters, businesses, documents and all numbers are invented;
Boston place names are used fictitiously.

Inspired by and calibrated against the Millbrook City RAG Challenge
  (c) William Caban — used with permission. All content fictional,
  AI-generated synthetic data. The Millbrook corpus itself is NOT
  redistributed here.

Merged in from our own earlier scaffold ("i-dont-know", same authors):
  eval/questions_boston.json — 10 evaluation questions over the real 311
    export, each with ground truth computed in pandas and the expression
    recorded in `verified_by`
  the frozen-control-group design (baseline/freeze.py, baseline/naive_boston.py)
    and the LIMIT fairness rule

Original work in this repository (civic/, eval/, app/, docs/, and the
--pipeline modification to the starter's judge) is Apache-2.0, same as the
starter.
